--TEST--
an added property has no constructor to set it, so a stored one with no default, no `?` type and no `lateinit` is refused, `readonly` and `static` are refused, and a write to a property with only a `get` hook does not compile (`rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

use Core\Time\Date;
use Shop\DateTools;

extend Date as DateTools {
    public int $count;

    public readonly int $limit;

    public static int $made = 0;

    public bool $isFirst {
        get => $this->day() == 1;
    }
}

var $day = Date::at(2026, 9, 1);
$day->isFirst = false;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
%Aerror[E0338]: an `extend` block cannot add a stored property with no default
%Aerror[E0338]: an `extend` block cannot add a `readonly` property
%Aerror[E0338]: an `extend` block cannot add a `static` property
%A
